WEBVTT

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.450
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.900
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:34.350
There are many kinds of penguins!

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.440
Yes...

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:42.960
Yes.

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:45.330
Okay.

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:48.140
Okay, but...

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:50.260
Yes.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:52.360
Okay.

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:54.800
We'll go in first.

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:58.260
What did Miss Sasako say?

00:01:58.790 --> 00:02:00.720
She said the ocean is very pretty.

00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:03.640
Why is she at the ocean?

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:06.680
She said she hasn't taken the train in a while

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:08.640
and got on the wrong one.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:16.250
Mr. Penguin is late, too.

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:20.280
He's probably running away 
from the Miss Penkos again.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:27.090
It's hard to even remember 
all of their names

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:28.500
since there are seven of them.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:39.260
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.030
Who's that?

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:43.240
Miss Penko number 8?

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:44.180
Oh, stop it.

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:46.640
This is my nephew.

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:49.180
Hello.

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:51.590
He's so cute!

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:56.150
Baby emperor penguins are so cute.

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:59.030
Oh, you're here, too.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:00.280
What?!

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:02.490
Miss Penko number 8?

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:03.850
Would you cut that out?

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:07.080
Is this a friend of 
yours, Mr. Penguin?

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:09.210
How rude!

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:12.040
Don't compare me to the likes 
of an emperor penguin!

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:14.440
That's <i>my</i> line!

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:15.460
Huh?

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:19.420
You're not both emperor penguins?

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:20.670
No!

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:23.100
I am the true emperor penguin!

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:25.930
I am the true king penguin!

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:28.770
Don't compare me to something 
with such an oversized head!

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:29.810
Ow!

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:32.110
I'm the one that doesn't want 
to be compared with <i>you</i>,

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:34.850
with your flashy orange king penguin color!

00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:36.980
It's elegant, not flashy!

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:37.860
Ow!

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:40.360
It appears they don't get along.

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:42.740
We're peace-loving,

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:45.950
but the king penguins are 
always picking fights with us.

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:48.610
You're the ones to blame!

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:52.920
You emperor penguins are always 
causing us so much trouble!

00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:55.330
Trouble?

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:58.000
Yes! For example...

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:03.090
King penguins work so 
much harder at the zoo,

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:06.330
We went to the zoo!                         (It was so hot!)

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:06.330
The emperor penguins were out walking! 

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:04.940
but humans are always

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:06.350
confusing us with emperor penguins!

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:08.310
It's indeed trouble!

00:04:09.070 --> 00:04:12.270
I guess there's a lot that 
penguins go through.

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:16.470
Well, the adults may 
look somewhat alike,

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:20.630
but the baby king penguins 
resemble dirty mops.

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:22.240
How rude!

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:23.070
Ow!

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:24.620
Stop being so violent!

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:27.160
Oh, who's that?

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:30.330
He's my son.

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:31.700
Isn't he cute?

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:36.500
Actually, rather than cute...

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:39.480
...he's a little scary.

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:40.730
How rude!

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:43.330
It's called adorably ugly!

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:45.570
H-Hey there...

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:48.010
Sorry I compared you to a mop.

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:53.480
Fluffy...

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:56.020
Puffy...

00:04:56.490 --> 00:04:58.190
Fluffy...

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:00.940
Puffy...

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:03.310
Fluffy...

00:05:03.310 --> 00:05:05.920
They seem to be getting along.

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:08.120
How about you two get along, too?

00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:11.870
W-Well, I am a pacifist at heart.

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:16.170
Oh, fine. Just this once, I'll call a truce.

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:21.130
South Pole Peace Treaty

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:18.430
Thank goodness.

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:21.130
The South Pole peace treaty 
has been enacted.

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:23.920
Oh, hey, it's an emperor penguin.

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:25.280
Wow, it is!

00:05:29.730 --> 00:05:31.990
Wow!

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:34.100
Pool! Pool!

00:05:34.450 --> 00:05:35.420
Pool!

00:05:34.450 --> 00:05:37.280
It's big enough even for me.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:37.310
Pool!

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:41.800
I've gained weight lately 
with all my drinking,

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:43.510
so I'd better swim a lot today.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:46.120
There you are, Mr. Penguin!

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:48.990
Mr. Penguin, how could you?

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:51.030
Why didn't you invite me?

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:55.670
Now, here is our question.

00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:59.710
What number from the right 
is Miss Penjolina?

00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:02.670
That's pretty hard.

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:06.130
Why are you here?

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:09.090
Heading to the pool today with Polar Bear and crew!

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:09.090
You announced it with your 
smartphone this morning.

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:12.900
Look after my nephew!

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:14.290
He's getting away!

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:18.140
Wait!

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:20.760
Looks like Mr. Penguin will 
be able to swim a lot today.

00:06:20.390 --> 00:06:21.980
Mr. Penguin!

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:31.950
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:23.230
I'm Penko.

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:24.140
I'm Penmi.

00:06:24.140 --> 00:06:24.960
I'm Penno.

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:25.800
I'm Penka.

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:26.720
I'm Penna.

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:27.710
I'm Penuelle.

00:06:27.710 --> 00:06:28.970
I'm Penjolina.

00:06:28.970 --> 00:06:31.950
I'm—

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:30.070
I'm Penka.

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:31.950
I'm Penna.

00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:37.340
That's not a stuffed penguin, is it?

00:06:37.340 --> 00:06:38.860
Let's talk to it.

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:41.650
Don't! He'll poke your eyes out!

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:48.180
Panda!

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:51.290
We came to the pool. 
Come out here and swim!

00:06:51.290 --> 00:06:52.850
Let's swim!

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:58.310
What? I just came to cool off.

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:00.970
If you eat then sleep, you'll get fat.

00:07:00.970 --> 00:07:02.230
You'll get fat!

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:04.420
That's fine!

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:07.480
I hate exercise!

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:09.640
Mr. Polar Bear!

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:11.490
Let's play together!

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:13.810
Sure.

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:16.300
Yay!

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:16.910
Try to get some exercise.

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:21.660
Ahh, this is paradise!

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:23.450
It's an emperor penguin!

00:07:23.450 --> 00:07:26.380
No! I'm a king penguin!

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:28.390
What? But you're an emperor penguin.

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:35.920
Jeez! Why do the humans 
mistake us all the time?!

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:38.990
Why is it king and emperor, anyway?

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:43.060
I don't want to talk 
about it much, but...

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:46.110
A long, long time ago,

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:49.800
when humans still couldn't 
go to the South Pole...

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:53.790
<i>It's so big! What a big penguin!</i>

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:57.990
<i>The ultimate penguin, the king.</i>

00:07:57.990 --> 00:07:59.790
Let us name it the king penguin.

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:05.230
King

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:03.980
At the time, the biggest 
penguins humans saw

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:05.250
were us, the king penguins.

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:08.710
Wow, how cool.

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:09.710
And?

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:13.680
After that, when humans were able 
to travel to the South Pole...

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:17.350
<i>Those</i> guys just happened to be there.

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:18.780
<i>Wow, they're huge!</i>

00:08:18.780 --> 00:08:21.310
<i>These guys are bigger than 
king penguins, Captain!</i>

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:22.810
<i>What should we name them?</i>

00:08:23.070 --> 00:08:26.180
<i>Well, how about emperor penguin,</i>

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:28.270
<i>since emperor is above king?</i>

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:29.530
What?!

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:31.860
That easily?

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:33.200
Exactly!

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:35.760
Humans made up this name for us,

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:38.240
and they still mistake us for emperors.

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:40.340
So infuriating.

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:45.420
Oh, it's not a big deal.

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:50.430
They say that life is full 
of mountains and valleys.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:53.010
Mountains have bamboo.

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:56.430
When you're hungry,
 there's bamboo and bamboo grass.

00:08:57.890 --> 00:08:59.150
You piss me off!

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:00.890
You totally piss me off!

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:06.410
Stop!

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:08.460
Piss me off!

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:11.890
Oh, Panda!

00:09:11.890 --> 00:09:13.780
Look! He's exercising!

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:15.470
Looks like fun!

00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:19.120
Wait!

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:21.090
Oh, Mr. Penguin!

00:09:21.090 --> 00:09:23.350
Mr. Penguin is exercising, too!

00:09:23.350 --> 00:09:25.080
Looks like fun!

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:28.130
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:27.300
I'm—

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:27.450
I'm Penjolina!

00:09:28.350 --> 00:09:30.010
You're the most popular of all!

00:09:30.010 --> 00:09:32.240
You would never understand how I feel!

00:09:36.290 --> 00:09:37.510
Hello!

00:09:38.270 --> 00:09:39.970
More penguins?

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:43.420
I'm the lover of the South Pole,
 Adélie penguin.

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:46.890
I'm stoic and modest, Chinstrap penguin.

00:09:47.340 --> 00:09:50.360
I have a stylish personality, Gentoo penguin.

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:53.840
The three of us make up
the Pygoscelis genus!

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:56.320
Genus Pygoscelis

00:09:56.660 --> 00:09:58.100
We totally pulled that off.

00:09:58.100 --> 00:09:59.060
Totally.

00:10:01.320 --> 00:10:03.180
P-Pygo?

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:04.720
Pygoscelis!

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:07.290
Your genus is too hard to say!

00:10:07.720 --> 00:10:10.580
It's been a while, Miss King Penguin!

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:15.260
Your Aptenodytes genus is much harder to say.

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:17.630
Are you getting along with the emperor penguin,

00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:20.440
who is also from the Aptenodytes genus?

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:24.890
His misleading name is always 
causing me trouble.

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:28.230
Our names are rather appropriate, too.

00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:30.230
Really?

00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:32.690
Adélie Penguin

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:33.120
The namesake for us Adélie penguins

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:36.450
is the name of an explorer's wife.

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:38.670
So even the males are Adélie.

00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:43.300
We are named Chinstrap penguins

00:10:42.850 --> 00:10:46.790
Chinstrap Penguin

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:45.270
due to our chinstraps...

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:46.790
Wow.

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:52.110
Gentoo Penguin

00:10:46.990 --> 00:10:49.300
We Gentoo penguins

00:10:49.300 --> 00:10:50.830
got our name from the white

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:52.390
pattern on our head which looks like a turban.

00:10:52.390 --> 00:10:56.260
So they took the Portuguese 
word for "gentile."

00:10:56.910 --> 00:10:59.410
That really is simple.

00:10:59.410 --> 00:11:01.870
Looks like you've been 
through a lot, too.

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:04.300
How about it, Panda?

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:06.220
Have you memorized us now?

00:11:06.860 --> 00:11:07.980
What?

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:10.550
Help...

00:11:09.370 --> 00:11:10.550
Hey! 
Penguin!

00:11:11.010 --> 00:11:12.140
...me!

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:13.420
Penguin!

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:13.420
Wait!

00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:16.220
Help!

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:16.220
Penguin!

00:11:17.470 --> 00:11:19.170
Do you remember which one is which?

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:23.570
It's a bit hard.

00:11:23.570 --> 00:11:26.910
Not to mention there are 18 
different types of penguins.

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:28.310
What?!

00:11:28.310 --> 00:11:29.660
But it's not a problem!

00:11:30.030 --> 00:11:33.160
That's why we have these penguin cards!

00:11:34.940 --> 00:11:37.050
Fun, yet educational!

00:11:37.410 --> 00:11:40.510
Currently for the special, 
low price of 500 yen!

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:42.380
Why are you trying to 
sell that right now?!

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:48.930
Main Gate

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:51.010
Trains are so difficult.

00:11:51.430 --> 00:11:55.530
There're things like limited express trains, 
and commuter express trains.

00:11:56.440 --> 00:11:58.400
Why can't they be like buses and

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:00.460
stop when you push a button...

00:12:11.670 --> 00:12:14.500
Why is the emperor's card 
the ultimate card?!

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:15.310
I don't know!

00:12:15.310 --> 00:12:17.000
Mr. Polar Bear!

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:18.230
There!

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:19.720
Over here!

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:19.720
There!

00:12:25.620 --> 00:12:26.930
I'm going to swim!

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:40.900
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:12:37.850 --> 00:12:40.340
What is Baisen?!

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:48.810
So good!

00:12:48.810 --> 00:12:52.340
The parfaits at Polar Bear's 
Café are awesome!

00:12:55.980 --> 00:12:57.400
Huh?

00:12:57.400 --> 00:12:59.240
You're not Mr. Penguin.

00:12:59.240 --> 00:13:00.590
Oh, hi. I'm...

00:13:01.330 --> 00:13:02.550
I call him Human.

00:13:03.190 --> 00:13:06.010
You're not wrong, 
Mr. Polar Bear, but...

00:13:06.700 --> 00:13:08.230
His name is Masaki.

00:13:08.670 --> 00:13:10.480
Do you want your usual, Panda?

00:13:11.370 --> 00:13:13.270
Yes, please. Coffee.

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:14.890
I'll have it black today.

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:17.760
Wow, Mr. Panda. You're getting coffee?

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:19.160
So stoic.

00:13:20.050 --> 00:13:22.440
Call me the Panda that 
knows the difference.

00:13:23.640 --> 00:13:26.910
Isn't black coffee bitter 
and not that good?

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:30.190
It's not not that good.

00:13:31.090 --> 00:13:33.370
It's because I'm the Panda 
that knows the difference.

00:13:33.930 --> 00:13:36.870
What? But it's bitter, right?

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:38.750
Would you like to try some?

00:13:40.090 --> 00:13:42.790
The coffee at Polar Bear's 
Café is delicious.

00:13:57.740 --> 00:13:59.700
It really is good!

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:01.440
Right?

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:02.820
It smells really good!

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:06.370
It's amazing that you can pour 
a cup of coffee like this!

00:14:06.890 --> 00:14:10.450
The secret of the deliciousness 
is in the baisen.

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:12.790
Baisen? What's that?

00:14:17.420 --> 00:14:18.710
That's seafood <i>(kaisen)</i>!

00:14:20.480 --> 00:14:22.590
That's a match <i>(taisen)</i>!

00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:26.260
That's an arcade <i>(ge-sen)</i>!

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:29.180
What the heck is baisen?!

00:14:29.490 --> 00:14:32.680
Baisen refers to coffee roasting.

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:34.590
Coffee roasting?

00:14:34.590 --> 00:14:38.590
The beans we get are 
roasted by a master.

00:14:38.590 --> 00:14:39.960
Master?

00:14:40.350 --> 00:14:43.150
Wow, I had no idea.

00:14:43.670 --> 00:14:45.830
I wanna meet them!

00:14:45.830 --> 00:14:47.610
I wouldn't mind taking you.

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:49.290
Really?!

00:14:51.920 --> 00:14:53.780
It's a little far, though.

00:14:54.950 --> 00:14:56.380
Is it overseas?

00:14:56.380 --> 00:14:58.540
Brazil? Colombia?

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:02.710
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:08.300
We're finally here.

00:15:09.440 --> 00:15:11.190
Mr. Polar Bear...

00:15:11.190 --> 00:15:12.090
Yes?

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:14.470
It's super close!

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:17.400
Yes, that's why it's only a little far.

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:27.780
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:29.790
Hello.

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:33.740
Oh, Mr. Polar Bear.

00:15:34.070 --> 00:15:37.700
Mama Red Squirrel, 
we'd like to see the master.

00:15:38.100 --> 00:15:42.350
I'm sorry. He's a little 
busy right now.

00:15:42.900 --> 00:15:45.110
So the squirrels are the roasters.

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:47.210
They're just part-time mothers.

00:15:48.820 --> 00:15:50.130
Oh, is that him?

00:15:50.420 --> 00:15:54.550
Yes. That's the master, 
Mr. Tree Kangaroo.

00:16:09.020 --> 00:16:10.230
All right.

00:16:13.350 --> 00:16:14.550
What is it?

00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:18.580
Mr. Tree Kangaroo, Masaki here...

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:20.520
I want to be your pupil!

00:16:20.520 --> 00:16:21.000
What?!

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:23.670
I want to be your pupil, too!

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:24.710
Huh?

00:16:24.990 --> 00:16:26.860
Oh, I don't recommend it.

00:16:26.860 --> 00:16:29.340
Coffee roasting is a pretty boring job.

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:31.000
We're only part-time but...

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:32.360
You need patience...

00:16:32.360 --> 00:16:33.880
And it's all manual labor.

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:36.600
Then I don't wanna.

00:16:36.950 --> 00:16:38.970
You had no intention to be 
his pupil to begin with.

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:40.310
Yep.

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:42.520
I'm totally serious.

00:16:43.420 --> 00:16:46.610
After having coffee at 
Polar Bear's Café today,

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:51.020
it was the first time I ever 
thought black coffee was good.

00:16:55.280 --> 00:17:00.420
I'd like to make that kind 
of delicious coffee myself.

00:17:07.180 --> 00:17:08.230
It's not possible.

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:11.340
Apparently he doesn't take pupils.

00:17:13.560 --> 00:17:14.800
All right.

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:15.790
What?!

00:17:16.730 --> 00:17:17.720
Really?!

00:17:18.480 --> 00:17:19.220
Yeah.

00:17:19.480 --> 00:17:22.140
A-All right!

00:17:22.840 --> 00:17:25.600
Well, you can stop by for a while.

00:17:26.210 --> 00:17:27.060
I'll do my best!

00:17:34.660 --> 00:17:36.860
Master! Thank you for accepting me!

00:17:36.860 --> 00:17:37.490
My name is Masaki!

00:17:38.020 --> 00:17:41.300
All right. The Red Squirrels 
will teach you.

00:17:41.300 --> 00:17:41.910
Yes, sir!

00:17:44.970 --> 00:17:46.600
The beans look white...

00:17:46.600 --> 00:17:47.830
or actually, a pale green.

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:48.880
Are they moldy?

00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:52.820
This is an unroasted coffee bean.

00:17:52.820 --> 00:17:54.140
Unroasted coffee bean?

00:17:54.140 --> 00:17:56.360
It turns brown once you roast it.

00:17:56.360 --> 00:17:57.760
Oh, I see.

00:17:58.190 --> 00:18:01.600
First, we'll show you how 
to separate the beans.

00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:02.310
Right.

00:18:04.630 --> 00:18:08.270
Before we start roasting, 
we take out the bad beans.

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:10.300
One bean at a time?!

00:18:10.300 --> 00:18:12.870
If you don't take them out, 
the coffee will taste bad.

00:18:12.870 --> 00:18:15.240
Wow, that's a lot of work.

00:18:15.610 --> 00:18:18.100
The bad beans are...

00:18:18.100 --> 00:18:19.660
like these where bugs ate part of them.

00:18:21.290 --> 00:18:22.580
And these rotten ones.

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:26.950
Make sure you don't over look 
these and get all of them.

00:18:26.950 --> 00:18:28.040
Yes, ma'am.

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:30.540
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:18:39.240 --> 00:18:41.320
Hey! Take out the big ones, too!

00:18:41.650 --> 00:18:43.720
Why? Aren't the big ones good?

00:18:45.160 --> 00:18:48.160
The big beans would 
cause uneven roasting!

00:18:50.280 --> 00:18:52.370
We're going to go through all of these?

00:18:52.370 --> 00:18:53.790
Yes, all today.

00:18:53.790 --> 00:18:54.850
Seriously?!

00:18:54.850 --> 00:18:56.520
Come on, hurry up!

00:18:56.520 --> 00:18:57.240
Yes, ma'am!

00:19:03.040 --> 00:19:04.300
You're too slow.

00:19:04.300 --> 00:19:05.310
Sorry!

00:19:07.190 --> 00:19:08.710
Pick up the pace!

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:10.030
Yes, ma'am!

00:19:13.110 --> 00:19:15.090
With more rhythm!

00:19:17.060 --> 00:19:18.810
What the heck?!

00:19:19.180 --> 00:19:22.380
I wanted to be 
Mr. Tree Kangaroo's pupil!

00:19:23.920 --> 00:19:25.790
The newbie has no right to complain!

00:19:25.790 --> 00:19:28.060
Move your hands, not your mouth!

00:19:28.510 --> 00:19:29.820
Yes, ma'am...

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:31.850
Pick up the pace!

00:19:31.850 --> 00:19:33.920
Masaki, your hands aren't moving!

00:19:33.920 --> 00:19:35.150
They are moving!

00:19:39.920 --> 00:19:42.440
I wonder how Masaki is doing.

00:19:42.810 --> 00:19:44.140
Who's that?

00:19:44.140 --> 00:19:45.080
What?

00:19:45.430 --> 00:19:47.400
The guy who was moved by the

00:19:47.400 --> 00:19:49.290
black coffee you recommended, right?

00:19:49.800 --> 00:19:50.890
Oh.

00:19:50.890 --> 00:19:52.320
What do you mean, "oh"?

00:19:52.860 --> 00:19:56.530
I'm a bad guy, so I 
don't look at my past.

00:19:56.980 --> 00:19:58.660
Can I get a café mocha?

00:20:06.030 --> 00:20:08.080
Thank you for the food!

00:20:13.460 --> 00:20:14.740
Hey, Masaki.

00:20:15.760 --> 00:20:18.150
How about some volleyball
 to work off that food?

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:20.510
Sure.

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:22.360
Polar Bear's Café

00:20:23.360 --> 00:20:25.300
It's ready!

00:20:26.670 --> 00:20:28.200
This is the net.

00:20:28.690 --> 00:20:30.790
It's more realistic than I thought.

00:20:31.200 --> 00:20:32.880
Let's start the game!

00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:34.500
Here I go!

00:20:37.100 --> 00:20:38.510
Center!

00:20:41.120 --> 00:20:41.970
Attack!

00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:45.810
Nice play!

00:20:45.810 --> 00:20:48.980
Ow! Okay, now I'm serious!

00:20:52.070 --> 00:20:53.810
Here we go, Masaki!

00:20:54.370 --> 00:20:55.400
Bring it!

00:20:59.180 --> 00:21:00.320
Yay!

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:01.690
Nice play!

00:21:11.730 --> 00:21:13.000
So,

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:16.110
how did things turn out 
with the Miss Penkos?

00:21:16.110 --> 00:21:18.320
Please don't remind me of that?

00:21:18.320 --> 00:21:19.950
Can I get another café mocha?

00:21:20.630 --> 00:21:23.970
Why don't you try the black 
coffee sometime, Mr. Penguin?

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:26.340
I don't need anymore 
bitterness in my life.

00:21:26.750 --> 00:21:27.950
Here you go, black coffee.

00:21:28.340 --> 00:21:29.260
It's on the house.

00:21:30.250 --> 00:21:32.230
It's bitter, right?

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:36.730
Oh, Mr. Tree Kangaroo.

00:21:36.730 --> 00:21:38.110
Here you go, your beans.

00:21:38.790 --> 00:21:40.510
Thank you for all of your hard work.

00:21:40.510 --> 00:21:42.610
Is Masaki working hard?

00:21:43.040 --> 00:21:48.570
Yeah. Well, he seems to have gotten 
in with the Red Squirrels.

00:21:50.740 --> 00:21:53.840
Yay! Straight wins!

00:21:55.910 --> 00:21:58.040
O-One more time!

00:22:00.370 --> 00:22:02.050
Oh, it's good.

00:22:02.590 --> 00:22:03.510
Right?

00:22:04.170 --> 00:22:06.990
It's mild with a refreshing finish.

00:22:06.990 --> 00:22:09.530
Such a mediocre comment.

00:22:09.530 --> 00:22:10.560
What?!

00:22:10.560 --> 00:22:11.410
Agreed.

00:22:11.410 --> 00:22:11.970
What?!

00:22:12.480 --> 00:22:14.850
You'd fail as a gourmet reporter.

00:22:14.850 --> 00:22:15.900
Hey, wait a minute.

00:22:15.900 --> 00:22:19.370
Mr. Penguin, when did you 
become a gourmet reporter?

00:22:19.370 --> 00:22:20.540
Today.

00:22:19.980 --> 00:22:21.240
I did not!

00:22:21.240 --> 00:22:24.280
So you aren't a reporter, 
but you're acting like one?

00:23:54.950 --> 00:24:24.460
Next Time

00:23:58.130 --> 00:23:59.750
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin!

00:23:59.750 --> 00:24:01.080
What is it, Panda?

00:24:01.080 --> 00:24:03.050
We can really see how petty you are

00:24:03.050 --> 00:24:06.380
from the top of that tree.

00:24:06.380 --> 00:24:08.450
You can see a lot more 
besides that, can't you?

00:24:08.450 --> 00:24:10.100
Then let's view the truth

00:24:10.100 --> 00:24:12.620
you want to hide from 
the top of the tree.

00:24:12.620 --> 00:24:14.400
Stop talking so profoundly.

00:24:14.400 --> 00:24:16.270
And why do you keep saying, "tree"? 
Where are we?

00:24:16.270 --> 00:24:17.310
Let's end this.

00:24:17.310 --> 00:24:19.110
Next week's Polar Bear Café,

00:24:19.110 --> 00:24:20.560
will be presented to you 
with just Mr. Penguin.

00:24:20.560 --> 00:24:21.770
We're all going to be there.

00:24:21.770 --> 00:24:22.910
Enjoy!

00:24:21.770 --> 00:24:24.440
The Ideal Single Living
